Adds structured session telemetry to `src/services/pilotMetrics.ts` and extends the pilot CSV schema to capture per-session drawing intelligence.

## New API

- **`SessionSummary`** — new interface capturing: sheet count, total detected wall count, distinct floor count, scale calibration confidence distribution (`auto` / `manual` / `none`), and time-to-3D-render in ms
- **`sessionSummary(drawings, renderTimeMs): SessionSummary`** — derives all metrics from the drawing array; floor count uses stored `floorNumber` falling back to filename inference; scale confidence buckets by whether `scaleMmPerPx` + `scaleNotation` are present

```ts
const summary = sessionSummary(drawings, renderTimeMs)
// {
//   sheetCount: 3, wallCount: 47, floorCount: 2,
//   scaleConfidenceDistribution: { auto: 2, manual: 1, none: 0 },
//   renderTimeMs: 4800
// }
```

## CSV schema extension

`PilotMetricRow` gains six new columns inserted after `time_to_usable_3d_min`:

| column | type | notes |
|---|---|---|
| `wall_count` | number | total `parsedWalls` across all drawings |
| `floor_count` | number | distinct floor levels |
| `scale_confidence_auto` | number | notation-derived scale |
| `scale_confidence_manual` | number | user-set scale, no notation |
| `scale_confidence_none` | number | uncalibrated sheets |
| `render_time_ms` | number | raw ms for tooling; `time_to_usable_3d_min` now also auto-filled |

`pilot/pilot_metrics_template.csv` header and sample row updated to match.

## Integration

`buildPilotSnapshot(drawings, renderTimeMs?)` delegates to `sessionSummary` internally — fully backwards-compatible (optional second arg, defaults to `0`).

## Summary

Adds Phase 24F: a local, docs-only Dixie host issue / first-PR handoff draft.

This packet prepares a paste-ready future `loa-dixie` issue body for consuming the Phase 24C/24D Straylight host scaffold, while keeping the actual Dixie filing and implementation as a future, separate event.

## What changed

Created:

- `docs/handoffs/phase-24f-dixie-host-issue-draft.md`

Updated:

- `docs/handoffs/README.md`

## Phase 24F scope

The new handoff draft defines a narrow future first-PR scope for `loa-dixie`:

- scaffold-consumption only;
- consume / model the six host handler contracts;
- explicitly inject `TenantResolver`;
- optionally wire / model `IntakeDenyLog`;
- surface typed refusals verbatim;
- preserve Phase 24C/24D host semantics;
- keep Dixie as inspect / relay / render only.

The draft intentionally does **not** bind a transport shape. HTTP routes, NATS subjects, RPC methods, BFF routes, or other operator-facing surfaces remain future Dixie-side decisions.

## Boundary

This PR is docs-only.

It does not:

- edit `src/`;
- edit `tests/`;
- edit `fixtures/`;
- edit `scripts/`;
- edit package files;
- edit specs or ADRs;
- edit Dixie, Finn, Freeside, or Hounfour repos;
- file an issue against `loa-dixie`;
- open a sibling-repo PR;
- post GitHub comments;
- add endpoints, routes, HTTP, NATS, RPC, Discord, or Telegram surfaces;
- re-export `src/straylight/host/` through `src/straylight/index.ts`;
- adopt Hounfour #116;
- consume Hounfour `main` or unpublished commits;
- import the Hounfour five-step corpus;
- adopt `0xhoneyjar:straylight:*`;
- adopt the Hounfour `recall-wedge` conformance category;
- implement vector 9;
- implement vectors 10–11;
- add public commitment-root behavior.

